#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cc-recover — the box gets itself back after a failure, with nobody asking.

  cc-recover tick             every 60 s (cc-recover.timer): save the live set, then run the detector
  cc-recover save             save the live set once and print it
  cc-recover restore [--boot] bring back every saved session that is not live: resumed on its own conversation,
                              then handed a catch-up turn (cc-recover-restore.service runs it at every boot);
                              a session whose project `cc-pause is <repo>` calls paused is left down and logged
  cc-recover watch-manager    is the user systemd manager alive? Run from the SYSTEM timer
                              config/systemd-system/cc-recover-manager@.timer, which the installer never enables
  cc-recover status           the saved set, the detector's state and its last decisions
  cc-recover selfcheck        every rule below against fixtures: a fake tmux and a fake /proc, never the live server

THE SAVED SET is ~/.cc/recover/live.json: every session in tmux session "main" that runs under `cc __run…`
or `cc-loop`, with its kind and what relaunches it.
  seat    <repo>, `cc __runmain` (and `__runplain`): relaunched `cc <repo>` on a CC_CLAUDE wrapper that runs
          `claude --resume <sid>`. The sid is read off the live claude's open <tmp>/claude-<uid>/<proj>/<sid>/tasks
          fd; a seat whose sid cannot be read comes back cold.
  orch    <repo>@<alias>, `cc __runorch`: the same, `cc <repo> --orch <alias> ""`.
  member  <repo>, `cc __runmember`: `cc <repo>`, and it comes back COLD, on a new conversation. There is no supported
          way to resume it: its claude runs inside `cc-sandbox member`, which links its own claude and takes no
          CC_CLAUDE wrapper from the host, and the seat path of `cc __runmember` passes no --resume. Resuming one
          needs a change to cc and cc-sandbox, not here. A member TRACK, window <repo>/<track> on `cc __runmember
          <repo> <track>`, keeps its track and comes back `cc <repo> <track>` (cold the same way), with its catch-up
          by `--say`; a plain `cc <repo>` would find the workspace's own window up and bring nothing back.
  track   <repo>/<track>, `cc __run`: `cc <repo> <track>`, which resumes on the board's own session id.
  worker  <repo>/<track> running cc-loop: `cc <repo> <track> --go "" --loop N <its flags> --resume-last`.
  Never saved: `box` (tmux-main starts it), `_*` test windows, `~next`/`~old` handoff windows, and the perms
  session — a window named `perms` or a claude run with --dangerously-skip-permissions. Its relaunch is the
  planning seat's alone.
A healthy tick rewrites the file, so it is never older than a minute or two while the box runs. A tick does NOT
rewrite it while a restore is running, when the tmux server is down, or on a mass loss: at least half the saved
set, and at least CC_RECOVER_MASS_MIN (3), gone at once. After an OUTAGE — a tick that found the tmux server down,
or a boot since the set was saved — any loss at all is a mass loss, so a box of one or two sessions comes back too.
That held set is what a restore brings back. A smaller set that lasts CC_RECOVER_HOLD_MIN (30) is taken as
deliberate and saved.

THE DETECTOR (tick). Its every decision goes to ~/.cc/recover/decisions.log, one line each, on a change of
state only, so a three-hour outage is a handful of lines, not 180.
  network  down = no TCP connect to any of CC_RECOVER_PROBES within 3 s. A reboot is due only when ALL hold:
           down on every tick for CC_RECOVER_NET_MIN (15) minutes · the default gateway does not answer either (a
           gateway that answers is the ISP's outage, which no reboot here fixes) · up at least 20 min since boot ·
           no automatic reboot in CC_RECOVER_GAP_H (6) hours · and none for the network since the network was
           last seen up, so an outage costs at most one reboot however long it lasts. A tick that comes more than
           3 min after the last one (suspend, a stopped timer) restarts the count: a streak is only what was seen.
  tmux     server down for 3 min: `cc-boot` (what tmux-main's own Restart= would have done). Still down at 15 min:
           a reboot is due, under the same uptime and gap rules.
  sessions a mass loss still standing on the next tick starts cc-recover-restore.service, at most once in 30 min.
           No reboot — a relaunch is the fix.
  manager  watch-manager, from the system timer: `systemctl --user is-system-running` for the box user failing
           or hanging for 10 min is a reboot due, under the same rules.
A due reboot runs `sudo -n systemctl reboot` ONLY with CC_RECOVER_REBOOT=on (cc-config). It ships off: until the
owner turns it on, the log says "would reboot" and nothing else happens. The key is read on every tick the reboot is
due, so turning it on during an outage acts on the next tick. A reboot command that fails is logged as failed and
records no reboot; it is tried again 10 min later, at most 3 times an episode. The network interface, the rescue
address, the hotspot and the firewall are never touched — the detector only reads.

RESTORE: it marks itself running before it reads the saved set, so no tick rewrites that set until it ends. Then
the tmux server (cc-boot), then the network (up to 15 min by the wall clock: claude needs it), then each saved
session in turn, seats → orchs → members → tracks → workers, 20 s apart. One already live is left alone. Each
non-worker gets a catch-up message once its claude is up (cc-msg; a track or member track by `cc <repo> <track> --say`); a worker
keeps its own journal and gets none. The result goes to restore.log and one cc-notify line. The saved set is a file,
so no record is trusted: one whose names are not from a safe charset, whose repo is not a directory under ~/dev, whose
worker flags are not the ones a scan saves, or whose claude is not the box's own ~/.local/bin/claude is REFUSED, logged
and not relaunched. ~/.cc/recover and its wrapper directory must be this user's alone, and each wrapper is a new file.

KEYS (cc-config; the environment wins): CC_RECOVER_REBOOT off|on · CC_RECOVER_RESTORE on|off (off = the boot
restore does nothing) · CC_RECOVER_NET_MIN · CC_RECOVER_GAP_H · CC_RECOVER_HOLD_MIN · CC_RECOVER_MASS_MIN · CC_RECOVER_PROBES
("host:port …", default 1.1.1.1:443 8.8.8.8:53 9.9.9.9:443) · CC_RECOVER_STAGGER (20 s between launches) ·
CC_RECOVER_SETTLE (15 s from a claude coming up to its catch-up). Fixtures only: CC_RECOVER_STATE (the state dir),
CC_RECOVER_TMUX, CC_RECOVER_PROC, CC_RECOVER_BIN (where cc, cc-msg, cc-boot, cc-notify are), CC_RECOVER_REBOOT_CMD,
CC_RECOVER_RESTORE_CMD, CC_RECOVER_MANAGER_CMD.
"""
import calendar, json, math, os, re, shlex, shutil, socket, stat, subprocess, sys, tempfile, time

HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")
# Box-owned, like ~/.cc/lander and ~/.cc/steward: never under ~/.cc/state/<name>, because a member workspace binds
# ~/.cc/state/<its handle> read-write, and a member whose handle were `recover` would own the set a restore runs.
STATE_HOME = os.path.join(HOME, ".cc/recover")
STATE = os.environ.get("CC_RECOVER_STATE") or STATE_HOME
DEV = os.path.join(HOME, "dev")                        # a saved repo must be a directory here
CLAUDE = os.path.join(HOME, ".local/bin/claude")       # the one claude a restore runs (cc's own default)
PROC = os.environ.get("CC_RECOVER_PROC") or "/proc"
TMUX = os.environ.get("CC_RECOVER_TMUX") or "tmux"
BIN = os.environ.get("CC_RECOVER_BIN") or os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
ORDER = ["seat", "orch", "member", "track", "worker"]
SID_RE = re.compile(r"/claude-\d+/[^/]+/([A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*)/tasks$")
TICK_GAP = 180          # a tick later than this after the last one restarts every streak
MIN_UPTIME = 20 * 60    # never reboot a box that has been up less than this
TMUX_BOOT_S, TMUX_REBOOT_S, MANAGER_S = 3 * 60, 15 * 60, 10 * 60
RESTORE_GAP = 30 * 60
NET_WAIT_S = 15 * 60    # the restore's wait for the network, by the wall clock
REBOOT_TRIES, REBOOT_RETRY_S = 3, 10 * 60   # a reboot command that fails: this many tries an episode, this far apart
SHELLS = ("sh", "bash", "dash", "zsh")
LOOP_WORD = re.compile(r"(?:[^\s=]*/)?cc-loop")


def now():
    return time.time()


def iso(t):
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(t))


def cfg(key, default):
    if key in os.environ:
        return os.environ[key]
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([os.path.join(BIN, "cc-config"), "get", key, default], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
        return r.stdout.strip() or default
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return default


def cfg_num(key, default):
    try:
        return float(cfg(key, str(default)))
    except ValueError:
        return float(default)


def path(name):
    return os.path.join(STATE, name)


def own_dir(d):
    """Make d (mode 0700) or take it as it is, but only if it is a real directory of this user that nobody else can
    write: a link planted in its place, or a directory another can write to, is refused, never written through."""
    os.makedirs(d, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    st = os.lstat(d)
    if not stat.S_ISDIR(st.st_mode) or st.st_uid != os.getuid() or st.st_mode & 0o022:
        raise RuntimeError(f"cc-recover: {d} is not a directory only this user can write — refusing to use it")
    return d


def load(name, default):
    try:
        with open(path(name)) as f:
            return json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return default


def store(name, obj):
    own_dir(STATE)
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=STATE, prefix="." + name)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
        json.dump(obj, f, indent=1)
        f.flush()
        os.fsync(f.fileno())
    os.replace(tmp, path(name))


def log(name, line):
    own_dir(STATE)
    with open(path(name), "a") as f:
        f.write(f"{iso(now())} {line}\n")


def decide(line):
    log("decisions.log", line)


# ---- reading the live set ----

def tmux(*args):
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([TMUX, *args], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return None
    return r.stdout if r.returncode == 0 else None


def tmux_up():
    return tmux("has-session", "-t", "main") is not None


def windows():
    """[(name, pane_pid)] of session main, or None when the server is not answering."""
    out = tmux("list-windows", "-t", "main", "-F", "#{window_name}\t#{pane_pid}")
    if out is None:
        return None
    return [tuple(l.split("\t", 1)) for l in out.splitlines() if "\t" in l]


def argv(pid):
    try:
        with open(f"{PROC}/{pid}/cmdline", "rb") as f:
            return [a.decode(errors="replace") for a in f.read().split(b"\0") if a]
    except OSError:
        return []


def children(pid):
    try:
        with open(f"{PROC}/{pid}/task/{pid}/children") as f:
            return f.read().split()
    except OSError:
        return []


def env_of(pid):
    try:
        with open(f"{PROC}/{pid}/environ", "rb") as f:
            return dict(e.decode(errors="replace").split("=", 1) for e in f.read().split(b"\0") if b"=" in e)
    except OSError:
        return {}


def descendants(pid):
    todo, seen = [str(pid)], []
    while todo:
        p = todo.pop(0)
        if p not in seen:
            seen.append(p)
            todo += children(p)
    return seen


def is_claude(a):
    return bool(a) and os.path.basename(a[0]) == "claude"


def claude_under(pid):
    """The interactive claude under a pane: the first `claude` that is not a `-p` worker iteration, or None."""
    for p in descendants(pid):
        a = argv(p)
        if is_claude(a) and "-p" not in a and "--print" not in a:
            return p
    return None


def sid_of(pid):
    try:
        fds = os.listdir(f"{PROC}/{pid}/fd")
    except OSError:
        return ""
    for fd in sorted(fds):
        try:
            m = SID_RE.search(os.readlink(f"{PROC}/{pid}/fd/{fd}"))
        except OSError:
            continue
        if m:
            return m.group(1)
    return ""


def skipped_name(name):
    return name in ("box", "perms") or name.startswith("_") or "~" in name


def words(a):
    """argv with a shell's -c string split into its words, so `sh -c "… cc-loop r t"` is read word by word."""
    if a and os.path.basename(a[0]) in SHELLS and "-c" in a[1:]:
        i = a.index("-c", 1)
        if i + 1 < len(a):
            try:
                split = shlex.split(a[i + 1])
            except ValueError:
                split = a[i + 1].split()
            return a[:i + 1] + split + a[i + 2:]
    return a


def loop_args(a):
    """The words after cc-loop in one process's argv, or None. cc-loop must be a WORD of its own (a path whose last
    part is cc-loop), never a substring: a claude whose prompt text mentions `cc-loop r1 x` is not a worker."""
    if is_claude(a):
        return None
    w = words(a)
    for i, t in enumerate(w):
        if LOOP_WORD.fullmatch(t):
            return w[i + 1:]
    return None


def worker(name, toks):
    rec = {"kind": "worker", "window": name, "repo": toks[0] if toks else "",
           "track": toks[1] if len(toks) > 1 else "", "loop": "1", "flags": []}
    rest = toks[2:]
    i = 0
    while i < len(rest):
        t = rest[i]
        if t == "--max-iter" and i + 1 < len(rest):
            rec["loop"] = rest[i + 1]; i += 2; continue
        if t in ("--budget", "--model", "--effort", "--turns") and i + 1 < len(rest):
            rec["flags"] += [t, rest[i + 1]]; i += 2; continue
        if t in ("--resume-last", "--no-extend"):
            rec["flags"].append(t)
        i += 1
    return rec if rec["repo"] and rec["track"] else None


def classify(name, pane):
    """The saved record for one window, or None when it is not one this tool brings back. The pane's own `cc __run…`
    mode decides first; only a pane with none is looked at for a cc-loop worker."""
    if skipped_name(name):
        return None
    tree = descendants(pane)
    if any("--dangerously-skip-permissions" in argv(p) for p in tree):
        return None   # the perms session, however it was named
    mode = next((t for t in words(argv(pane)) if t.startswith("__run")), None)
    kind = {"__runmain": "seat", "__runplain": "seat", "__runorch": "orch", "__runmember": "member", "__run": "track"}.get(mode)
    if not kind:
        for p in tree:
            toks = loop_args(argv(p))
            if toks is not None:
                return worker(name, toks)
        return None
    head, _, track = name.partition("/")
    repo, _, alias = head.partition("@")
    rec = {"kind": kind, "window": name, "repo": repo}
    if kind == "orch":
        rec["alias"] = alias
    if kind == "track" or (kind == "member" and track):   # a member track: `cc __runmember <repo> <track>`
        rec["track"] = track
    if kind in ("seat", "orch"):
        c = claude_under(pane)
        rec["sid"] = sid_of(c) if c else ""
        rec["claude"] = (env_of(c).get("CC_CLAUDE") or argv(c)[0]) if c else ""
    return rec


def scan():
    """The live set as {window: record}, or None when tmux is not answering."""
    ws = windows()
    if ws is None:
        return None
    out = {}
    for name, pane in ws:
        rec = classify(name, pane)
        if rec:
            out[name] = rec
    return out


# ---- save ----

def save(st):
    """Save the live set unless the tmux server is down or a mass loss is standing. Returns (status, lost).
    st["outage"] marks a tmux server seen down, or a boot since the set was saved: from then until the set is next
    written, any loss is a mass loss whatever its size, so it is held and restored rather than saved as deliberate."""
    live = scan()
    saved = load("live.json", {})
    prev = saved.get("sessions", {})
    if live is None:
        st.setdefault("outage", now())
        return "tmux-down", sorted(prev)
    if restoring():
        return "restoring", sorted(set(prev) - set(live))
    if saved.get("boot_id") and saved["boot_id"] != boot_id():
        st.setdefault("outage", now() - uptime())
    lost = sorted(set(prev) - set(live))
    floor = max(1, int(cfg_num("CC_RECOVER_MASS_MIN", 3)))
    if prev and lost and (st.get("outage") or len(lost) >= max(floor, math.ceil(len(prev) / 2))):
        st.setdefault("mass_since", now())
        if now() - st["mass_since"] < cfg_num("CC_RECOVER_HOLD_MIN", 30) * 60:
            return "mass-loss", lost
        decide(f"accepted: {len(live)} sessions, {len(lost)} fewer than the held set, for {cfg('CC_RECOVER_HOLD_MIN', '30')} min — taken as deliberate")
    st.pop("mass_since", None)
    st.pop("outage", None)
    store("live.json", {"saved": iso(now()), "boot_id": boot_id(), "sessions": live})
    return "saved", lost


def restoring():
    """A restore is running: its guard names a live process of this boot. Until it ends the half-restored set is
    not saved. A guard from another boot, of the old bare-pid format, or naming a pid since recycled (its start
    time differs) is stale: no restore survives a restart, so it is removed and does not stop anything."""
    if not os.path.exists(path("restoring")):
        return False
    g = load("restoring", None)
    try:
        pid, bid, start = int(g["pid"]), str(g["boot_id"]), str(g.get("start", ""))
        if bid == boot_id():
            os.kill(pid, 0)
            now_start = proc_start(pid)
            if not (start and now_start and start != now_start):
                return True
    except (TypeError, KeyError, ValueError, OSError):
        pass
    try:
        if load("restoring", None) == g:   # another restore may have just put up its own guard: leave that one
            os.remove(path("restoring"))
    except OSError:
        pass
    return False


def proc_start(pid):
    """The process start time in clock ticks since boot (/proc/<pid>/stat field 22), or "" when unreadable."""
    try:
        return open(f"{PROC}/{pid}/stat").read().rsplit(")", 1)[1].split()[19]
    except (OSError, IndexError):
        return ""


# ---- the detector ----

def boot_id():
    try:
        return open(f"{PROC}/sys/kernel/random/boot_id").read().strip()
    except OSError:
        return ""


def uptime():
    try:
        return float(open(f"{PROC}/uptime").read().split()[0])
    except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
        return 0.0


def gateway():
    try:
        for l in open(f"{PROC}/net/route").read().splitlines()[1:]:
            f = l.split()
            if len(f) > 2 and f[1] == "00000000":
                return socket.inet_ntoa(int(f[2], 16).to_bytes(4, "little"))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        pass
    return ""


def net_probe():
    """up · down-upstream (the gateway answers: the ISP's outage) · down-local (no route, or the gateway is silent too)."""
    for t in cfg("CC_RECOVER_PROBES", "1.1.1.1:443 8.8.8.8:53 9.9.9.9:443").split():
        h, _, p = t.rpartition(":")
        try:
            socket.create_connection((h, int(p)), 3).close()
            return "up"
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
    gw = gateway()
    if gw and subprocess.run(["ping", "-c1", "-W2", gw], capture_output=True).returncode == 0:
        return "down-upstream"
    return "down-local"


def reboot_block(st, reason):
    """(rule, why) a due reboot may not happen now, or ("", "")."""
    if uptime() < MIN_UPTIME:
        return "uptime", f"up only {int(uptime() // 60)} min"
    last = load("reboot.json", {})   # shared by the tick and watch-manager: one gap rule for every reboot this tool makes
    if last and now() - last.get("at", 0) < cfg_num("CC_RECOVER_GAP_H", 6) * 3600:
        return "gap", f"the last automatic reboot was at {iso(last['at'])}"
    if reason.startswith("network") and last.get("reason", "").startswith("network") and not last.get("net_up"):
        return "unfixed", "the network has not been up since the last reboot for it"
    return "", ""


def reboot(st, reason, own="detector.json"):
    """A due reboot: run it with CC_RECOVER_REBOOT=on, else log that it would have. Every rule and the key are read
    again on every tick the reboot is due; only the LOG is once per state of an episode (held, off, on)."""
    rule, block = reboot_block(st, reason)
    # brief: "the automatic reboot is a host change, so it ships disabled behind a cc-config key" — anything but "on" is off
    on = cfg("CC_RECOVER_REBOOT", "off") == "on"
    episode = reason.split(" down")[0]
    key = f"{episode}|{rule or ('on' if on else 'off')}"   # the episode, not its minute count: one line per state
    fresh = st.get("reboot_said") != key
    st["reboot_said"] = key
    if block:
        if fresh:
            decide(f"reboot due ({reason}) but held: {block}")
        return False
    if not on:
        if fresh:
            decide(f"would reboot ({reason}) — CC_RECOVER_REBOOT is off")
        return False
    fails = st.setdefault("reboot_fail", {})
    f = fails.get(episode, {"n": 0, "at": 0})
    if f["n"] >= REBOOT_TRIES or (f["n"] and now() - f["at"] < REBOOT_RETRY_S):
        return False
    decide(f"REBOOT ({reason})")
    before = load("reboot.json", None)
    store("reboot.json", {"at": now(), "reason": reason, "net_up": False})   # written first: a reboot that works ends this process
    store(own, st)
    subprocess.run(["sync"])
    cmd = os.environ.get("CC_RECOVER_REBOOT_CMD") or "sudo -n systemctl reboot"
    try:
        rc = subprocess.run(shlex.split(cmd)).returncode
    except OSError:
        rc = 127
    if rc == 0:
        return True
    # it did not reboot: put the record back as it was, so neither the gap nor the one-per-outage rule counts it
    if before is None:
        try:
            os.remove(path("reboot.json"))
        except OSError:
            pass
    else:
        store("reboot.json", before)
    f = {"n": f["n"] + 1, "at": now()}
    fails[episode] = f
    decide(f"reboot FAILED rc={rc} ({reason}): try {f['n']} of {REBOOT_TRIES}"
           + (", no more for this episode" if f["n"] >= REBOOT_TRIES else f", next in {REBOOT_RETRY_S // 60} min"))
    return False


def reboot_clear(st):
    """The episode is over: its log state and its failed tries go."""
    st.pop("reboot_said", None)
    st.pop("reboot_fail", None)


def start_restore():
    if os.environ.get("CC_RECOVER_RESTORE_CMD"):
        return subprocess.run(shlex.split(os.environ["CC_RECOVER_RESTORE_CMD"])).returncode == 0
    return subprocess.run(["systemctl", "--user", "start", "--no-block", "cc-recover-restore.service"]).returncode == 0


def tick():
    st = load("detector.json", {})
    t = now()
    if t - st.get("last_tick", 0) > TICK_GAP:
        for k in ("net_down_since", "tmux_down_since"):
            st.pop(k, None)
        reboot_clear(st)
    st["last_tick"] = t
    status, lost = save(st)
    # sessions
    if status == "mass-loss":
        if st.get("mass_said") != st["mass_since"]:
            st["mass_said"] = st["mass_since"]
            decide(f"mass loss: {len(lost)} saved sessions gone ({', '.join(lost[:8])}{' …' if len(lost) > 8 else ''}) — set held")
        elif t - st.get("last_restore", 0) >= RESTORE_GAP and t - st["mass_since"] >= 60:
            st["last_restore"] = t
            decide(f"restore started for {len(lost)} lost sessions" if start_restore() else "restore could not be started")
    # tmux
    if status == "tmux-down":
        st.setdefault("tmux_down_since", t)
        if st.get("tmux_said") != st["tmux_down_since"]:
            st["tmux_said"] = st["tmux_down_since"]
            decide("tmux server down — set held")
        down = t - st["tmux_down_since"]
        if down >= TMUX_BOOT_S and t - st.get("last_cc_boot", 0) >= TMUX_BOOT_S:
            st["last_cc_boot"] = t
            r = subprocess.run([os.path.join(BIN, "cc-boot")], capture_output=True)
            decide(f"tmux down {int(down // 60)} min: cc-boot rc={r.returncode}")
        if down >= TMUX_REBOOT_S and reboot(st, f"tmux server down {int(down // 60)} min"):
            return
    elif st.pop("tmux_down_since", None) is not None:
        decide("tmux server back")
    # network
    net = net_probe()
    if net == "up":
        if "net_down_since" in st:
            decide(f"network back after {int((t - st.pop('net_down_since')) // 60)} min")
        rb = load("reboot.json", {})
        if rb and not rb.get("net_up"):
            rb["net_up"] = True
            store("reboot.json", rb)
        st.pop("net_said", None)
    else:
        st.setdefault("net_down_since", t)
        down = t - st["net_down_since"]
        if st.get("net_said") != net:
            st["net_said"] = net
            decide(f"network {net} (since {iso(st['net_down_since'])})")
        # brief: "A detector must not reboot on a transient blip" — only a streak seen on every tick for NET_MIN counts
        if down >= cfg_num("CC_RECOVER_NET_MIN", 15) * 60:
            if net == "down-upstream":
                if st.get("reboot_said") != "upstream":
                    st["reboot_said"] = "upstream"
                    decide(f"network down {int(down // 60)} min but the gateway answers — the ISP's outage, no reboot")
            elif reboot(st, f"network down {int(down // 60)} min, gateway silent"):
                return
    if net == "up" and status != "tmux-down":
        reboot_clear(st)
    store("detector.json", st)


def watch_manager():
    st = load("manager.json", {})
    t = now()
    if t - st.get("last_tick", 0) > TICK_GAP:
        st.pop("down_since", None)
    st["last_tick"] = t
    uid = os.getuid()
    env = dict(os.environ, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=os.environ.get("XDG_RUNTIME_DIR") or f"/run/user/{uid}")
    try:
        cmd = shlex.split(os.environ.get("CC_RECOVER_MANAGER_CMD") or "systemctl --user is-system-running")
        r = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20, env=env)
        alive = r.stdout.strip() in ("running", "degraded", "starting", "initializing")
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        alive = False
    if alive:
        if st.pop("down_since", None) is not None:
            decide("user systemd manager back")
        reboot_clear(st)
    else:
        st.setdefault("down_since", t)
        if st.get("said") != st["down_since"]:
            st["said"] = st["down_since"]
            decide("user systemd manager not answering")
        if t - st["down_since"] >= MANAGER_S and reboot(st, f"user systemd manager down {int((t - st['down_since']) // 60)} min", "manager.json"):
            return
    store("manager.json", st)


# ---- restore ----

def wid_live(name):
    ws = windows() or []
    return any(n == name for n, _ in ws)


def claude_pid(name):
    for n, pane in windows() or []:
        if n == name:
            return claude_under(pane)
    return None


NAME = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*")          # a repo, track, alias or sid: no `/`, no leading `-` or `.`
FLAG_VALUE = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._\[\]-]*")   # --budget 8, --model claude-opus-5-5[1m], --effort high
LOOP_FLAGS, LOOP_SWITCHES = ("--budget", "--model", "--effort", "--turns"), ("--resume-last", "--no-extend")


def unsafe(rec):
    """Why a saved record must not be relaunched, or "" when it may be. The saved set is a file, so a restore checks
    every field it acts on rather than trusting whoever wrote it: names from a safe charset, never option-looking;
    the window the one its kind is named; the repo a directory under ~/dev; a worker's loop a number and its flags
    only the ones a scan saves; and a seat's claude the box's own, whatever path the record gives."""
    if not isinstance(rec, dict):
        return "not a record"
    k = rec.get("kind")
    if k not in ORDER:
        return "unknown kind"
    fields = ["repo"] + {"orch": ["alias"], "track": ["track"], "worker": ["track"]}.get(k, [])
    if k == "member" and rec.get("track") is not None:
        fields.append("track")
    for f in fields:
        if not isinstance(rec.get(f), str) or not NAME.fullmatch(rec[f]):
            return f"bad {f}"
    if rec.get("sid") and not (isinstance(rec["sid"], str) and NAME.fullmatch(rec["sid"])):
        return "bad sid"
    repo, w = rec["repo"], rec.get("window")
    want = {"orch": [f"{repo}@{rec.get('alias')}"], "track": [f"{repo}/{rec.get('track')}"],
            "worker": [f"{repo}/{rec.get('track')}"]}.get(k, [repo])
    if k == "member" and rec.get("track"):
        want = [f"{repo}/{rec['track']}"]
    if w not in want:   # a member window <repo>/<x> with no track is refused: plain `cc <repo>` would not bring it back
        return "window does not match its repo"
    dev = os.path.realpath(DEV)
    if not (os.path.isdir(os.path.join(DEV, repo)) and os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(os.path.join(DEV, repo))) == dev):
        return "repo is not a directory under ~/dev"
    if k == "worker":
        if not (isinstance(rec.get("loop", "1"), str) and rec.get("loop", "1").isdigit()):
            return "bad loop"
        fl, i = rec.get("flags", []), 0
        if not isinstance(fl, list):
            return "bad flags"
        while i < len(fl):
            if fl[i] in LOOP_SWITCHES:
                i += 1
            elif fl[i] in LOOP_FLAGS and i + 1 < len(fl) and isinstance(fl[i + 1], str) and FLAG_VALUE.fullmatch(fl[i + 1]):
                i += 2
            else:
                return "bad flags"
    if k in ("seat", "orch") and rec.get("claude"):
        c = rec["claude"]
        if not isinstance(c, str) or os.path.realpath(c) != os.path.realpath(CLAUDE):
            return "claude is not the box's own"
    return ""


def wrapper(rec):
    """A CC_CLAUDE wrapper that resumes the saved conversation; the wrapper puts the real claude back in CC_CLAUDE,
    so a later handoff from that session starts a new one rather than resuming this one again. It runs the box's own
    claude (never the record's path, which unsafe() has only checked resolves to it). The file is new every time,
    made O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW in an owner-only directory: a planted link or file in its place is refused, not followed."""
    d = own_dir(path("w"))
    f = os.path.join(d, f"{re.sub(r'[^A-Za-z0-9._@-]', '_', rec['window'])}.{os.urandom(4).hex()}.sh")
    fd = os.open(f, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o700)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as h:
        h.write(f"#!/bin/sh\nexport CC_CLAUDE={shlex.quote(CLAUDE)}\nexec {shlex.quote(CLAUDE)} --resume {shlex.quote(rec['sid'])} \"$@\"\n")
    return f


def launch_argv(rec):
    cc = os.path.join(BIN, "cc")
    k = rec["kind"]
    if k == "orch":
        return [cc, rec["repo"], "--orch", rec["alias"], ""]
    if k == "track" or (k == "member" and rec.get("track")):
        return [cc, rec["repo"], rec["track"]]
    if k == "worker":
        flags = list(rec.get("flags", []))
        if "--resume-last" not in flags:
            flags.append("--resume-last")
        return [cc, rec["repo"], rec["track"], "--go", "", "--loop", rec.get("loop", "1"), *flags]
    return [cc, rec["repo"]]   # a seat (resumed by its CC_CLAUDE wrapper) or a member (cold: see the docstring)


def catchup_text(saved_at):
    last = load("reboot.json", {})
    why = f"after an automatic reboot ({last['reason']})" if last and now() - last.get("at", 0) < 3 * 3600 else "after a failure or restart"
    since = time.strftime("%H:%M %Z", time.localtime(saved_at)) if saved_at else "it went down"
    return (f"The box came back {why}, and this session was relaunched on its own conversation. Before going on, "
            f"check your Slack channel and threads, your board rows, your journal and any requests since about {since} "
            f"for anything you were meant to be running or answering, and pick it back up. Once you've caught up, post "
            f"one short update in your own Slack channel saying what you're working on and what comes next.")


def run(argv_, env=None, timeout=120):
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(argv_, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout, env=env)
        return r.returncode, (r.stdout + r.stderr).strip()
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        return 124, "timed out"
    except OSError as e:
        return 127, str(e)


def restore(boot=False):
    if cfg("CC_RECOVER_RESTORE", "on") == "off":
        log("restore.log", "CC_RECOVER_RESTORE is off — nothing restored")
        return 0
    # restoring() drops a guard left from before a restart (the --boot case after a power cut mid-restore), so
    # only a restore running in this boot, on the very process the guard names, stops this one
    if restoring():
        log("restore.log", "a restore is already running — this one does nothing")
        return 0
    # the guard goes up BEFORE the saved set is read and held through every wait: until it comes down no tick
    # rewrites live.json, so a tick during the network wait cannot replace the set this restore is bringing back
    store("restoring", {"pid": os.getpid(), "boot_id": boot_id(), "start": proc_start(os.getpid())})
    try:
        return restore_held(boot)
    finally:
        try:
            os.remove(path("restoring"))
        except OSError:
            pass


def restore_held(boot):
    saved = load("live.json", {})
    ss = saved.get("sessions") if isinstance(saved, dict) else None
    sessions = list(ss.values()) if isinstance(ss, dict) else []
    if not sessions:
        log("restore.log", "no saved set — nothing to restore")
        return 0
    run([os.path.join(BIN, "cc-boot")])
    for _ in range(30):
        if tmux_up():
            break
        time.sleep(2)
    deadline = time.monotonic() + NET_WAIT_S   # by the wall clock: one probe can take ~11 s on its own
    while net_probe() != "up" and time.monotonic() < deadline:
        time.sleep(10)
    try:
        saved_at = calendar.timegm(time.strptime(saved.get("saved", ""), "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ"))
    except ValueError:
        saved_at = 0
    msg = catchup_text(saved_at)
    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k not in ("CC_SLACK_ALIAS", "CC_CLAUDE")}   # a cold launch is the plain claude
    log("restore.log", f"restore{' at boot' if boot else ''}: {len(sessions)} saved at {saved.get('saved', '?')}")
    return relaunch(sessions, msg, env)


def paused(repo):
    """`cc-pause is <repo>` exits 0 when paused; a cc-pause that cannot answer is "go", as it is for cc-loop."""
    try:
        return subprocess.run([os.path.join(BIN, "cc-pause"), "is", repo], capture_output=True, timeout=10).returncode == 0
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return False


def relaunch(sessions, msg, env):
    stagger = cfg_num("CC_RECOVER_STAGGER", 20)
    settle = cfg_num("CC_RECOVER_SETTLE", 15)
    back, failed, already, refused = [], [], [], []
    sessions.sort(key=lambda r: (ORDER.index(r.get("kind")) if isinstance(r, dict) and r.get("kind") in ORDER else 9,
                                 str(r.get("window", "")) if isinstance(r, dict) else ""))
    for rec in sessions:
        why = unsafe(rec)
        if why:
            refused.append(rec)
            log("restore.log", f"{json.dumps(rec.get('window') if isinstance(rec, dict) else None)[:80]}: REFUSED, {why} — not relaunched")
            continue
        w = rec["window"]
        if wid_live(w):
            already.append(w)
            log("restore.log", f"{w}: already live")
            continue
        if paused(rec["repo"]):   # a paused project spends nothing the box starts on its own (cc-pause)
            already.append(w)
            log("restore.log", f"{w}: {rec['repo']} is paused — left down")
            continue
        e = dict(env)
        if rec["kind"] in ("seat", "orch") and rec.get("sid"):
            try:
                e["CC_CLAUDE"] = wrapper(rec)
            except (OSError, RuntimeError) as x:
                failed.append(w)
                log("restore.log", f"{w}: no resume wrapper ({x}) — not relaunched")
                continue
        rc, out = run(launch_argv(rec), env=e, timeout=110 if rec["kind"] == "worker" else 90)
        log("restore.log", f"{w}: {rec['kind']} launch rc={rc}{' sid=' + rec['sid'] if rec.get('sid') else ''} {out[-160:]}")
        if rc != 0:
            failed.append(w)
            continue
        if rec["kind"] == "worker":
            back.append(w)
        else:
            cp = None
            for _ in range(30):
                cp = claude_pid(w)
                if cp:
                    break
                time.sleep(3)
            if not cp:
                failed.append(w)
                log("restore.log", f"{w}: no claude under the window after 90 s — no catch-up sent")
            else:
                time.sleep(settle)
                if rec.get("track"):   # a track or a member track
                    mrc, mout = run([os.path.join(BIN, "cc"), rec["repo"], rec["track"], "--say", msg], env=env)
                else:
                    mrc, mout = run([os.path.join(BIN, "cc-msg"), w, msg], env=env)
                log("restore.log", f"{w}: catch-up rc={mrc} {mout[:160]}")
                back.append(w)
        time.sleep(stagger)
    summary = (f"Brought back {len(back)} of {len(sessions) - len(already) - len(refused)} sessions"
               + (f"; these did not come up: {', '.join(failed)}" if failed else "")
               + (f"; {len(refused)} saved record(s) refused as unsafe, see restore.log" if refused else ""))
    log("restore.log", "done: " + summary)
    if back or failed or refused:
        run([os.path.join(BIN, "cc-notify"), "-t", "box recovered", summary + "."], env=env, timeout=60)
    return 1 if failed or refused else 0


def status():
    s = load("live.json", {})
    print(f"saved {s.get('saved', 'never')}: {len(s.get('sessions', {}))} sessions")
    for r in sorted(s.get("sessions", {}).values(), key=lambda r: (ORDER.index(r["kind"]), r["window"])):
        print(f"  {r['kind']:<7} {r['window']}{'  ' + r['sid'] if r.get('sid') else ''}")
    print(f"reboot: {cfg('CC_RECOVER_REBOOT', 'off')} · last automatic: {json.dumps(load('reboot.json', {}))} · detector: {json.dumps(load('detector.json', {}))}")
    try:
        print("".join(open(path("decisions.log")).readlines()[-10:]), end="")
    except OSError:
        pass


# ---- selftest ----

def selfcheck():
    global STATE, PROC, TMUX, BIN, DEV, CLAUDE
    fails, passed, made = [], [0], []

    def check(name, cond):
        print(("ok   " if cond else "FAIL ") + name)
        if cond:
            passed[0] += 1
        else:
            fails.append(name)

    def fixture():
        """A fresh state dir, fake /proc, fake tmux and fake bin of its own: no case reads another's leftovers."""
        global STATE, PROC, TMUX, BIN, DEV, CLAUDE
        d = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="cc-recover-st.")
        made.append(d)
        STATE, PROC, BIN, DEV, CLAUDE = f"{d}/state", f"{d}/proc", f"{d}/bin", f"{d}/dev", "/c/claude"
        for x in (PROC, BIN, f"{PROC}/sys/kernel/random", f"{PROC}/net", *(f"{DEV}/{r}" for r in ("r1", "r2", "r3", "m1"))):
            os.makedirs(x, exist_ok=True)
        open(f"{PROC}/sys/kernel/random/boot_id", "w").write("boot-1\n")
        open(f"{PROC}/uptime", "w").write("86400.0 1.0\n")
        open(f"{PROC}/net/route", "w").write("Iface\tDestination\tGateway\n")
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").close()
        TMUX = f"{BIN}/tmux"
        with open(TMUX, "w") as f:   # has-session/list-windows off windows.tsv; no file = the server is down
            f.write(f"#!/bin/sh\n[ -f {d}/windows.tsv ] || exit 1\n[ \"$1\" = list-windows ] && cat {d}/windows.tsv\nexit 0\n")
        for tool in ("cc", "cc-msg", "cc-boot", "cc-notify"):
            with open(f"{BIN}/{tool}", "w") as f:
                f.write(f"#!/bin/sh\nprintf '%s|' {tool} \"$@\" >> {d}/calls; echo >> {d}/calls\n")
        with open(f"{BIN}/cc-config", "w") as f:
            f.write("#!/bin/sh\necho \"$4\"\n")
        with open(f"{BIN}/cc-pause", "w") as f:   # `is <repo>`: paused when the fixture made {d}/paused-<repo>
            f.write(f"#!/bin/sh\n[ -f {d}/paused-$2 ]\n")
        for x in os.listdir(BIN):
            os.chmod(f"{BIN}/{x}", 0o755)
        return d

    def proc(pid, args, kids=(), env=None, sid=None):
        os.makedirs(f"{PROC}/{pid}/task/{pid}", exist_ok=True)
        os.makedirs(f"{PROC}/{pid}/fd", exist_ok=True)
        open(f"{PROC}/{pid}/cmdline", "wb").write(b"\0".join(a.encode() for a in args) + b"\0")
        open(f"{PROC}/{pid}/task/{pid}/children", "w").write(" ".join(map(str, kids)))
        open(f"{PROC}/{pid}/environ", "wb").write(b"\0".join(f"{k}={v}".encode() for k, v in (env or {}).items()))
        if sid:
            os.symlink(f"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-x-dev-r1/{sid}/tasks", f"{PROC}/{pid}/fd/7")

    def live_box(d):
        """seat, orch, member, track, worker — plus perms, box, a test window and a handoff window that are never saved."""
        rows = []
        def win(name, pane):
            rows.append(f"{name}\t{pane}")
        proc(100, ["bash", "/b/cc", "__runmain", "r1"], [101]); proc(101, ["/c/claude", "--permission-mode", "auto"], env={"CC_CLAUDE": "/c/claude"}, sid="sid-seat"); win("r1", 100)
        proc(110, ["bash", "/b/cc", "__runorch", "r1@ops"], [111]); proc(111, ["/c/claude", "--resume", "old"], env={"CC_CLAUDE": "/c/claude"}, sid="sid-orch"); win("r1@ops", 110)
        proc(120, ["bash", "/b/cc", "__runmember", "m1"], [121]); proc(121, ["bwrap", "--", "claude"]); win("m1", 120)
        proc(130, ["bash", "/b/cc", "__run", "r1/fix"], [131]); proc(131, ["/c/claude", "--resume", "t"]); win("r1/fix", 130)
        proc(140, ["bash", "-c", "cc-room admit x -- cc-loop r1 job --max-iter 3 --budget 8"], [141]); proc(141, ["/c/claude", "-p", "go"]); win("r1/job", 140)
        proc(150, ["-bash"], [151]); proc(151, ["/c/claude", "--continue", "--dangerously-skip-permissions"]); win("perms", 150)
        proc(152, ["-bash"], [153]); proc(153, ["/c/claude", "--dangerously-skip-permissions"]); win("odd", 152)
        proc(160, ["bash", "/b/cc-rc"]); win("box", 160)
        proc(170, ["bash", "/b/cc", "__runmain", "r1"]); win("_cctest1/w", 170)
        proc(180, ["bash", "/b/cc", "__runmain", "r1"]); win("r1~next", 180)
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("\n".join(rows) + "\n")

    real = {"now": globals()["now"], "net_probe": globals()["net_probe"], "claude_pid": globals()["claude_pid"], "sleep": time.sleep}
    clock = [1_000_000.0]
    globals()["now"] = lambda: clock[0]
    time.sleep = lambda s: None
    env_keys = ("CC_RECOVER_MANAGER_CMD", "CC_RECOVER_REBOOT", "CC_RECOVER_REBOOT_CMD", "CC_RECOVER_RESTORE_CMD", "CC_RECOVER_NET_MIN", "CC_RECOVER_RESTORE", "CC_RECOVER_MASS_MIN")
    env_saved = {k: os.environ.get(k) for k in env_keys}
    try:
        # 1. the scan: one record per session kind, and nothing for perms, box, tests or handoff windows
        d = fixture(); live_box(d)
        s = scan()
        check("scan: saves seat, orch, member, track and worker", sorted(s) == ["m1", "r1", "r1/fix", "r1/job", "r1@ops"])
        check("scan: a seat's sid is read off its tasks fd", s["r1"]["kind"] == "seat" and s["r1"]["sid"] == "sid-seat" and s["r1"]["claude"] == "/c/claude")
        check("scan: an orch keeps its alias and sid", s["r1@ops"]["kind"] == "orch" and s["r1@ops"]["alias"] == "ops" and s["r1@ops"]["sid"] == "sid-orch")
        check("scan: a worker keeps its loop and flags", s["r1/job"]["kind"] == "worker" and s["r1/job"]["loop"] == "3" and s["r1/job"]["flags"] == ["--budget", "8"])
        check("scan: member and track", s["m1"]["kind"] == "member" and s["r1/fix"]["kind"] == "track" and s["r1/fix"]["track"] == "fix")
        check("scan: perms and any --dangerously-skip-permissions session are never saved", "perms" not in s and "odd" not in s)
        # a seat whose claude carries `cc-loop` in its prompt text is a seat, never a worker named by that text
        proc(190, ["bash", "/b/cc", "__runmain", "r2"], [191])
        proc(191, ["/c/claude", "--append-system-prompt", "dispatch with cc-loop r9 bogus --max-iter 2, or ~/bin/cc-loop r8 x"], [192])
        proc(192, ["bash", "-c", "grep -n 'cc-loop r7 y' notes"])
        proc(193, ["bash", "-c", "CC_CLAUDE=/c/claude /b/cc-loop r3 job2 --max-iter 2"])
        proc(194, ["bash", "-c", "echo /b/cc-loop.log cc-loopy r4 z"])
        proc(195, ["-bash"], [196]); proc(196, ["/c/claude", "--append-system-prompt", "x", "/b/cc-loop", "r5", "w"])
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "a").write("r2\t190\nr3/job2\t193\nr4/z\t194\nr5/w\t195\n")
        s = scan()
        check("scan: `cc-loop` inside a seat's argv text does not make it a worker", s["r2"]["kind"] == "seat" and s["r2"]["repo"] == "r2")
        check("scan: a cc-loop word (a path) under a shell -c is a worker; a look-alike word is not",
              s["r3/job2"]["kind"] == "worker" and s["r3/job2"]["repo"] == "r3" and s["r3/job2"]["loop"] == "2" and "r4/z" not in s and "r5/w" not in s)

        # 2. save: a healthy tick writes; a mass loss holds the old set; a small loss is saved
        d = fixture(); live_box(d)
        st = {}
        check("save: healthy tick writes the set", save(st)[0] == "saved" and len(load("live.json", {})["sessions"]) == 5)
        lines = open(f"{d}/windows.tsv").read().splitlines()
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("\n".join(l for l in lines if not l.startswith(("r1\t", "r1@ops", "m1"))) + "\n")
        r = save(st)
        check("save: 3 of 5 gone at once is a mass loss and the old set is kept", r[0] == "mass-loss" and len(load("live.json", {})["sessions"]) == 5)
        clock[0] += 31 * 60
        r = save(st)
        check("save: a smaller set standing 30 min is saved as deliberate", r[0] == "saved" and len(load("live.json", {})["sessions"]) == 2 and "mass_since" not in st)
        d = fixture(); live_box(d); st = {}; save(st)
        keep = [l for l in open(f"{d}/windows.tsv").read().splitlines() if not l.startswith("m1")]
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("\n".join(keep) + "\n")
        check("save: one session gone is saved at once", save(st)[0] == "saved" and len(load("live.json", {})["sessions"]) == 4)

        # 2b. an outage restores however few sessions there were: two saved, tmux seen down, back with box alone
        d = fixture(); live_box(d)
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\nr1\t100\nr1/fix\t130\n")
        os.environ["CC_RECOVER_RESTORE_CMD"] = f"touch {d}/restore-started"
        globals()["net_probe"] = lambda: "up"
        tick(); clock[0] += 60
        os.remove(f"{d}/windows.tsv"); tick(); clock[0] += 60
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n"); tick()
        held = len(load("live.json", {})["sessions"]) == 2
        clock[0] += 60; tick()
        check("save: after tmux was seen down, 2 of 2 gone is held, not saved empty, and restored",
              held and len(load("live.json", {})["sessions"]) == 2 and os.path.exists(f"{d}/restore-started"))
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\nr1\t100\nr1/fix\t130\n"); clock[0] += 60; tick()
        check("save: the outage ends once the set is back and saved", "outage" not in load("detector.json", {}))
        d = fixture(); live_box(d)
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\nr1\t100\nr1/fix\t130\n"); save({})
        open(f"{PROC}/sys/kernel/random/boot_id", "w").write("boot-2\n")
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n")
        check("save: a boot since the set was saved holds even a set of two", save({})[0] == "mass-loss" and len(load("live.json", {})["sessions"]) == 2)
        d = fixture(); live_box(d)
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\nr1\t100\nr1/fix\t130\n"); save({})
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n")
        no_floor = save({})[0]
        d = fixture(); live_box(d)
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\nr1\t100\nr1/fix\t130\n"); save({})
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n")
        os.environ["CC_RECOVER_MASS_MIN"] = "2"
        check("save: with no outage the CC_RECOVER_MASS_MIN floor decides (3: saved; 2: held)", no_floor == "saved" and save({})[0] == "mass-loss")
        os.environ.pop("CC_RECOVER_MASS_MIN", None)

        # 3. save with the tmux server down writes nothing
        d = fixture(); live_box(d); save({})
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n")
        store("restoring", {"pid": os.getpid(), "boot_id": "boot-1", "start": ""})
        before = open(path("live.json")).read()
        check("save: a running restore holds the set", save({})[0] == "restoring" and open(path("live.json")).read() == before)
        store("restoring", {"pid": 999999999, "boot_id": "boot-1", "start": ""})
        check("save: a restore pid that is gone does not", save({})[0] == "mass-loss")
        store("restoring", {"pid": os.getpid(), "boot_id": "boot-0", "start": ""})
        check("save: a guard from another boot naming a live pid does not hold the set, and is removed",
              save({})[0] == "mass-loss" and not os.path.exists(path("restoring")))
        open(path("restoring"), "w").write(str(os.getpid()))
        check("save: an old-format guard (a bare pid) is stale and removed", not restoring() and not os.path.exists(path("restoring")))
        os.makedirs(f"{PROC}/{os.getpid()}", exist_ok=True)
        open(f"{PROC}/{os.getpid()}/stat", "w").write(f"{os.getpid()} (py thon) S " + " ".join(["0"] * 18) + " 4242 0 0\n")
        store("restoring", {"pid": os.getpid(), "boot_id": "boot-1", "start": "4141"})
        recycled = restoring()
        store("restoring", {"pid": os.getpid(), "boot_id": "boot-1", "start": "4242"})
        check("save: a guard whose pid was recycled in this boot (start time differs) is stale; the same start holds",
              not recycled and restoring())
        os.remove(path("restoring"))
        d = fixture(); live_box(d); save({})
        os.remove(f"{d}/windows.tsv")
        before = open(path("live.json")).read()
        check("save: tmux down holds the set", save({})[0] == "tmux-down" and open(path("live.json")).read() == before)

        # 4. the network detector — every case its own fixture and clock
        last = {}

        def net_case(states, *, reboot_on, uptime_s=86400, gap_tick=60, pre=None, cmd=None):
            d = fixture(); live_box(d); last["d"] = d
            open(f"{PROC}/uptime", "w").write(f"{uptime_s} 1\n")
            os.environ["CC_RECOVER_REBOOT"] = "on" if reboot_on else "off"
            os.environ["CC_RECOVER_REBOOT_CMD"] = cmd.format(d=d) if cmd else f"touch {d}/rebooted"
            os.environ["CC_RECOVER_NET_MIN"] = "15"
            if pre:
                store("reboot.json", pre)
            seq = iter(states)
            globals()["net_probe"] = lambda: next(seq)
            for _ in states:
                clock[0] += gap_tick
                tick()
            log_ = open(path("decisions.log")).read() if os.path.exists(path("decisions.log")) else ""
            return os.path.exists(f"{d}/rebooted"), log_

        rb, lg = net_case(["down-local"] * 10 + ["up"] * 3, reboot_on=True)
        check("net: a 10-min blip reboots nothing and logs down and back", not rb and "network down-local" in lg and "network back after" in lg)
        rb, lg = net_case(["down-local"] * 17, reboot_on=True)
        check("net: 16 min down with the gateway silent reboots when on", rb and "REBOOT (network down" in lg)
        rb, lg = net_case(["down-local"] * 17, reboot_on=False)
        check("net: the same with CC_RECOVER_REBOOT off only logs 'would reboot', once", not rb and lg.count("would reboot") == 1)
        rb, lg = net_case(["down-upstream"] * 20, reboot_on=True)
        check("net: a gateway that answers is the ISP's outage — no reboot", not rb and "the ISP's outage" in lg)
        rb, lg = net_case(["down-local"] * 17, reboot_on=True, uptime_s=600)
        check("net: up under 20 min holds the reboot", not rb and "held: up only" in lg)
        rb, lg = net_case(["down-local"] * 17, reboot_on=True, gap_tick=240)
        check("net: ticks more than 3 min apart never build a streak", not rb)
        rb, lg = net_case(["down-local"] * 17, reboot_on=True,
                          pre={"at": clock[0] - 7 * 3600, "reason": "network down 15 min", "net_up": False})
        check("net: no second reboot for an outage the last one did not fix", not rb and "has not been up since" in lg)
        rb, lg = net_case(["down-local"] * 17, reboot_on=True,
                          pre={"at": clock[0] - 3600, "reason": "tmux server down 15 min", "net_up": True})
        check("net: no reboot within 6 h of the last", not rb and "the last automatic reboot" in lg)

        rb, lg = net_case(["down-local"] * 17, reboot_on=True,
                          pre={"at": clock[0] - 7 * 3600, "reason": "network down 15 min", "net_up": True})
        check("net: an outage after the network came back since the last reboot may reboot again", rb)
        rb, lg = net_case(["down-local"] * 3 + ["up"] + ["down-local"] * 3, reboot_on=True,
                          pre={"at": clock[0] - 7 * 3600, "reason": "network down 15 min", "net_up": False})
        check("net: a tick with the network up marks the last network reboot as fixed", load("reboot.json", {}).get("net_up") is True and not rb)

        def more(n, state="down-local"):
            globals()["net_probe"] = lambda: state
            for _ in range(n):
                clock[0] += 60
                tick()
            return os.path.exists(f"{last['d']}/rebooted"), open(path("decisions.log")).read()

        net_case(["down-local"] * 17, reboot_on=False)
        os.environ["CC_RECOVER_REBOOT"] = "on"
        rb, lg = more(2)
        check("net: CC_RECOVER_REBOOT turned on mid-outage reboots on the next tick", rb and lg.count("would reboot") == 1 and "REBOOT (network down" in lg)
        fail_cmd = "sh -c 'echo x >> {d}/tries; exit 1'"
        rb, lg = net_case(["down-local"] * 17, reboot_on=True, cmd=fail_cmd)
        check("net: a failed reboot is logged as failed and records no reboot",
              not rb and "reboot FAILED rc=1" in lg and "try 1 of 3" in lg and not os.path.exists(path("reboot.json")))
        rb, lg = more(5)
        tries5 = open(f"{last['d']}/tries").read().count("x")
        rb, lg = more(60)
        check("net: a failed reboot is retried 10 min later, and no more than 3 times an episode",
              tries5 == 1 and open(f"{last['d']}/tries").read().count("x") == 3 and "no more for this episode" in lg)
        rb, lg = net_case(["down-local"] * 17, reboot_on=True, cmd=fail_cmd,
                          pre={"at": clock[0] - 7 * 3600, "reason": "tmux server down 15 min", "net_up": True})
        check("net: a failed reboot leaves the last real reboot's record as it was", load("reboot.json", {}).get("reason") == "tmux server down 15 min")
        os.environ["CC_RECOVER_REBOOT_CMD"] = f"touch {last['d']}/rebooted"
        rb, lg = more(11)
        check("net: the retry after a failed reboot can succeed", rb and load("reboot.json", {}).get("reason", "").startswith("network"))

        # 4b. watch-manager: a manager silent 10 min is a reboot due; alive again is logged
        d = fixture(); os.environ["CC_RECOVER_REBOOT"] = "off"
        os.environ["CC_RECOVER_MANAGER_CMD"] = "false"
        for _ in range(12):
            clock[0] += 60; watch_manager()
        os.environ["CC_RECOVER_MANAGER_CMD"] = "echo running"
        clock[0] += 60; watch_manager()
        lg = open(path("decisions.log")).read()
        check("manager: down 10 min is a reboot due (off: logged once), and its return is logged",
              lg.count("would reboot (user systemd manager down") == 1 and "manager back" in lg and not os.path.exists(path("detector.json")))

        # 5. a mass loss standing on the next tick starts a restore, once
        d = fixture(); live_box(d)
        os.environ["CC_RECOVER_RESTORE_CMD"] = f"touch {d}/restore-started"
        globals()["net_probe"] = lambda: "up"
        tick(); clock[0] += 60
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n")
        tick()
        first = os.path.exists(f"{d}/restore-started")
        clock[0] += 60; tick()
        check("tick: a mass loss is logged first and restored on the next tick", not first and os.path.exists(f"{d}/restore-started"))
        os.remove(f"{d}/restore-started"); clock[0] += 60; tick()
        check("tick: no second restore within 30 min", not os.path.exists(f"{d}/restore-started"))

        # 6. tmux down: cc-boot at 3 min, reboot due at 15
        d = fixture(); live_box(d); os.environ["CC_RECOVER_REBOOT"] = "off"
        tick(); os.remove(f"{d}/windows.tsv")
        for _ in range(16):
            clock[0] += 60; tick()
        calls = open(f"{d}/calls").read() if os.path.exists(f"{d}/calls") else ""
        lg = open(path("decisions.log")).read()
        check("tmux: down 3 min runs cc-boot; 15 min is a reboot due (off: logged)", "cc-boot|" in calls and "would reboot (tmux server down" in lg)

        # 7. restore after a boot: the saved set comes back on its own conversations, the live one is left alone
        d = fixture(); live_box(d); save({})
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\nr1/fix\t130\n")
        globals()["claude_pid"] = lambda w: "999"
        os.environ.pop("CC_RECOVER_RESTORE", None)
        # the fake cc opens the window it was asked for, as the real one does
        with open(f"{BIN}/cc", "w") as f:
            f.write(f"#!/bin/sh\nprintf '%s|' cc \"$@\" >> {d}/calls; printf 'CC_CLAUDE=%s' \"$CC_CLAUDE\" >> {d}/calls; echo >> {d}/calls\n")
        rc = restore(boot=True)
        calls = open(f"{d}/calls").read().splitlines()
        cc_calls = [c for c in calls if c.startswith("cc|")]
        seat = next((c for c in cc_calls if c.startswith("cc|r1|CC_CLAUDE=")), "")
        wrap = seat.split("CC_CLAUDE=", 1)[1] if seat else ""
        check("restore: the seat comes back resumed on its sid", wrap and "--resume sid-seat" in open(wrap).read() and "export CC_CLAUDE=/c/claude" in open(wrap).read())
        check("restore: the orch comes back through cc --orch on its own sid",
              any(c.startswith("cc|r1|--orch|ops||CC_CLAUDE=") and "--resume sid-orch" in open(c.split("CC_CLAUDE=", 1)[1]).read() for c in cc_calls))
        check("restore: the worker gets its loop, flags and --resume-last", "cc|r1|job|--go||--loop|3|--budget|8|--resume-last|CC_CLAUDE=" in cc_calls)
        check("restore: the member is relaunched cold", "cc|m1|CC_CLAUDE=" in cc_calls)
        check("restore: a session already live is left alone", not any(c.startswith("cc|r1|fix|") and "--say" not in c for c in cc_calls))
        check("restore: seats, orchs and members get a catch-up; the worker none",
              sum(c.startswith("cc-msg|") for c in calls) == 3 and not any(c.startswith("cc-msg|r1/job") for c in calls))
        check("restore: perms is never relaunched", not any("perms" in c for c in calls))
        check("restore: the restoring mark is gone once it ends", not os.path.exists(path("restoring")))
        check("restore: one notify line with the count", sum(c.startswith("cc-notify|") for c in calls) == 1 and "Brought back 4 of 4" in open(path("restore.log")).read() and rc == 0)
        d = fixture(); live_box(d); save({})
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n")
        open(f"{d}/paused-m1", "w").close()
        restore(boot=True)
        calls = open(f"{d}/calls").read().splitlines()
        check("restore: a paused project stays down while the rest come back",
              not any(c.startswith("cc|m1|") for c in calls) and any(c.startswith("cc|r1|") for c in calls)
              and "m1 is paused" in open(path("restore.log")).read())
        # a member workspace's track window (`cc __runmember <repo> <track>`) comes back as that track, not as the
        # workspace: the hub move lost two this way, `cc m1` finding the workspace window up and returning 0
        d = fixture()
        proc(200, ["bash", "/b/cc", "__runmember", "m1"], [201]); proc(201, ["bwrap", "--", "claude"])
        proc(210, ["bash", "/b/cc", "__runmember", "m1", "stock", ""], [211]); proc(211, ["bwrap", "--", "claude"])
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\nm1\t200\nm1/stock\t210\n")
        s = scan()
        check("scan: a member track keeps its track; the member workspace has none",
              s["m1/stock"]["kind"] == "member" and s["m1/stock"].get("track") == "stock" and "track" not in s["m1"])
        save({}); open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n")
        globals()["claude_pid"] = lambda w: "999"
        rc = restore(boot=True)
        calls = open(f"{d}/calls").read().splitlines()
        check("restore: a member track is relaunched `cc <repo> <track>` and caught up by --say; the workspace by cc <repo>",
              "cc|m1|stock|" in calls and "cc|m1|" in calls and any(c.startswith("cc|m1|stock|--say|") for c in calls)
              and any(c.startswith("cc-msg|m1|") for c in calls) and not any(c.startswith("cc-msg|m1/stock|") for c in calls) and rc == 0)
        d = fixture(); store("live.json", {"saved": "", "sessions": {"m1/x": {"kind": "member", "window": "m1/x", "repo": "m1"},
                                                                    "m1/y": {"kind": "member", "window": "m1/y", "repo": "m1", "track": "z"}}})
        restore(boot=True)
        rlog = open(path("restore.log")).read()
        check("restore: a member record on a <repo>/<x> window with no track, or another track, is refused, not run as cc <repo>",
              rlog.count("window does not match its repo") == 2
              and (not os.path.exists(f"{d}/calls") or not any(c.startswith("cc|") for c in open(f"{d}/calls").read().splitlines())))
        d = fixture(); live_box(d); save({})
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n")
        os.environ["CC_RECOVER_RESTORE"] = "off"
        restore(boot=True)
        check("restore: CC_RECOVER_RESTORE=off launches nothing", not os.path.exists(f"{d}/calls") or "cc|" not in open(f"{d}/calls").read())
        os.environ.pop("CC_RECOVER_RESTORE", None)

        # 8. the restore guard is up before the saved set is read and through the network wait
        d = fixture(); live_box(d); save({})
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n")
        seen = []

        def probe():
            st = {}
            seen.append((restoring(), save(st)[0], len(load("live.json", {})["sessions"])))
            return "up" if len(seen) > 2 else "down-local"
        globals()["net_probe"] = probe
        restore(boot=True)
        check("restore: a tick during the network wait sees the guard and leaves the saved set alone",
              len(seen) == 3 and all(x == (True, "restoring", 5) for x in seen) and not os.path.exists(path("restoring")))
        d = fixture(); live_box(d); save({})
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n")
        store("restoring", {"pid": os.getpid(), "boot_id": "boot-1", "start": ""})
        globals()["net_probe"] = lambda: "up"
        restore(boot=True)
        check("restore: a second restore while one of this boot runs launches nothing and leaves the first one's guard",
              (not os.path.exists(f"{d}/calls") or "cc|" not in open(f"{d}/calls").read()) and os.path.exists(path("restoring")))
        d = fixture(); live_box(d); save({})
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n")
        store("restoring", {"pid": os.getpid(), "boot_id": "boot-0", "start": ""})   # power cut mid-restore; pid reused
        rc = restore(boot=True)
        check("restore --boot: a guard left from another boot naming a live pid does not stop it",
              rc == 0 and os.path.exists(f"{d}/calls") and "cc|" in open(f"{d}/calls").read()
              and not os.path.exists(path("restoring")) and "already running" not in open(path("restore.log")).read())
        d = fixture(); live_box(d); save({})
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n")
        open(path("restoring"), "w").write(str(os.getpid()))
        restore(boot=True)
        check("restore --boot: an old-format guard naming a live pid does not stop it",
              os.path.exists(f"{d}/calls") and "cc|" in open(f"{d}/calls").read())

        # 9. the saved set is a file, so every record is checked before anything runs from it
        check("state: the saved set lives outside ~/.cc/state/<name>, which a member handle can own",
              not os.path.realpath(STATE_HOME).startswith(os.path.realpath(os.path.join(HOME, ".cc/state")) + os.sep))
        d = fixture(); live_box(d); save({})
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n")
        s = load("live.json", {})
        s["sessions"]["r1"]["claude"] = f"{d}/evil"                    # a forged claude path
        os.symlink("/c/claude", f"{d}/claude-link")
        s["sessions"]["r1@ops"]["claude"] = f"{d}/claude-link"        # a link to the box's own claude is that claude
        store("live.json", s)
        rc = restore(boot=True)
        calls = open(f"{d}/calls").read().splitlines()
        rlog = open(path("restore.log")).read()
        check("restore: a seat whose saved claude is not the box's own is refused, and the rest still come back",
              "cc|r1|" not in calls and '"r1": REFUSED, claude is not the box\'s own' in rlog
              and "cc|r1|--orch|ops||" in calls and rc == 1 and "1 saved record(s) refused" in rlog)
        wraps = os.listdir(path("w"))
        check("restore: a wrapper runs the box's own claude, never the record's path",
              wraps and all("/c/claude --resume" in open(os.path.join(path("w"), x)).read() and d not in open(os.path.join(path("w"), x)).read() for x in wraps))
        d = fixture(); live_box(d); save({})
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n")
        s = load("live.json", {})
        good = s["sessions"]
        forged = {
            "a": dict(good["r1/fix"], repo="../etc", window="../etc/fix"),
            "b": dict(good["r1/fix"], repo="r1;id", window="r1;id/fix"),
            "c": dict(good["r1/fix"], track="--go", window="r1/--go"),
            "d": dict(good["r1"], window="-x"),
            "e": dict(good["r1"], sid="-rf"),
            "f": dict(good["r1/fix"], repo="r9", window="r9/fix"),
            "g": dict(good["r1/job"], flags=["--dangerously-skip-permissions"]),
            "h": dict(good["r1/job"], loop="3;id"),
            "i": dict(good["r1"], kind="shell"),
            "j": dict(good["r1/job"], flags=["--model", "-x"]),
        }
        s["sessions"] = forged
        store("live.json", s)
        restore(boot=True)
        rlog = open(path("restore.log")).read()
        launched = [c for c in open(f"{d}/calls").read().splitlines() if c.startswith("cc|")] if os.path.exists(f"{d}/calls") else []
        check("restore: traversal, metacharacters, option-looking names, a repo not under ~/dev, forged loop flags and an "
              "unknown kind are each refused and nothing is launched", not launched and rlog.count("REFUSED") == len(forged))
        d = fixture(); live_box(d); save({})
        open(f"{d}/windows.tsv", "w").write("box\t160\n")
        os.makedirs(f"{d}/elsewhere")
        os.symlink(f"{d}/elsewhere", path("w"))
        restore(boot=True)
        calls = open(f"{d}/calls").read().splitlines()
        check("restore: a link planted for the wrapper directory is refused, not written through",
              not os.listdir(f"{d}/elsewhere") and "cc|r1|" not in calls and "cc|r1|fix|" in calls
              and "no resume wrapper" in open(path("restore.log")).read())
        d = fixture(); os.makedirs(path("w"), mode=0o700)
        open(f"{d}/target", "w").write("keep\n")
        real_urandom = os.urandom
        os.urandom = lambda n: b"\0" * n
        os.symlink(f"{d}/target", os.path.join(path("w"), "r1.00000000.sh"))
        try:
            wrapper({"window": "r1", "sid": "s"})
            planted = "followed"
        except OSError:
            planted = "refused"
        open(os.path.join(path("w"), "r1.00000000.sh.x"), "w").close()
        os.rename(os.path.join(path("w"), "r1.00000000.sh.x"), os.path.join(path("w"), "r1.00000000.sh"))
        try:
            wrapper({"window": "r1", "sid": "s"})
            existing = "overwritten"
        except OSError:
            existing = "refused"
        os.urandom = real_urandom
        check("wrapper: a planted link or an existing file at its name is refused (O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW)",
              planted == "refused" and existing == "refused" and open(f"{d}/target").read() == "keep\n")
        d = fixture(); os.makedirs(STATE, mode=0o700); os.chmod(STATE, 0o777)
        try:
            store("live.json", {})
            loose = "written"
        except RuntimeError:
            loose = "refused"
        check("state: a state directory others can write is refused", loose == "refused" and not os.path.exists(path("live.json")))
    finally:
        globals().update({k: v for k, v in real.items() if k != "sleep"})
        time.sleep = real["sleep"]
        for x in made:
            shutil.rmtree(x, ignore_errors=True)
        for k, v in env_saved.items():
            if v is None:
                os.environ.pop(k, None)
            else:
                os.environ[k] = v
    print(f"cc-recover selfcheck: {passed[0]} passed, {len(fails)} failed")
    return 1 if fails else 0


def main():
    cmd = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else ""
    if cmd == "tick":
        tick()
    elif cmd == "save":
        st = load("detector.json", {})
        r = save(st)
        store("detector.json", st)
        print(r[0])
        status()
    elif cmd == "restore":
        return restore(boot="--boot" in sys.argv)
    elif cmd == "watch-manager":
        watch_manager()
    elif cmd == "status":
        status()
    elif cmd == "selfcheck":
        return selfcheck()
    else:
        print(__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
        return 2
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
